      "keysecondary": [],
      "comment": "Vautrin: The Trial in the Opera Epiclese",
      "content": "After Carole's death, Vautrin killed the hardliners who framed her. At the trial the crowd cheered for him, but Neuvillette, saying justice by law differs from personal justice, found him guilty and the Oratrice agreed. Vautrin raged, then said goodbye and went to the Fortress of Meropide.",
